---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { newest, entries } from '../data/entries';
const latest = newest[0];
const selected = newest.filter(e => e.milestone).slice(0, 3);
---
<Base title="Home">
  <section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">My game project / notes from along the way</p><h1>They Forgot the Alamo</h1><p class="lead">A man wakes up thinking he's Davy Crockett. He's got a shotgun, a room he can tear apart, and—where his hat ought to be—a raccoon. That's the game I'm trying to make.</p><p>The current build has a playable five-chapter desktop campaign and both endings. Latest update: October 3, 2026.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/play/">How to play</a><a class="button secondary" href="/devlog/">My project notes</a><a class="button secondary" href="/timeline/">See how it grew</a></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img src="/media/two-hand-carry.webp" alt="October 2 review capture of Davy holding the shotgun; the campaign grew beyond this room afterward" fetchpriority="high" /></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">What changed most recently</p><h2>Latest update</h2></div><a href="/devlog/">All my notes →</a></div><div class="split"><img src={latest.image || '/media/two-hand-carry.webp'} alt={latest.imageAlt || 'October 2 shotgun review capture; it predates the finished campaign'} loading="lazy" /><div><p class="date">{latest.date} / I was working on…</p><h3><a href={'/devlog/'+latest.slug+'/'}>{latest.title}</a></h3><p>{latest.summary}</p><a class="button secondary" href={'/devlog/'+latest.slug+'/'}>Read the note</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">A few big steps</p><h2>How it got here</h2></div><a href="/timeline/">See the whole timeline →</a></div><div class="grid">{selected.map(e => <a class="card milestone" href={'/devlog/'+e.slug+'/'}>{e.image && <img src={e.image} alt={e.imageAlt} loading="lazy" />}<div class="card-content"><span class="date">{e.date}</span><h3>{e.title}</h3><p>{e.summary}</p></div></a>)}</div></section>
  <section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Then / a later snapshot</p><h2>From boxes to Davy</h2><p>The earliest saved build uses simple shapes for Davy. Later versions add a character model, animation, and a shotgun grip that has had a frankly unreasonable number of reviews. The later image is from a weapon review, before the campaign was finished.</p><div class="comparison"><figure><img src="/media/first-commit-room.webp" alt="First surviving game build from September 29, reconstructed in a browser" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Then / saved September 29 build, reconstructed October 1</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/media/two-hand-carry.webp" alt="October 2 review capture of Davy's revised shotgun carry" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Later snapshot / October 2 weapon review, before the campaign finish</figcaption></figure></div></section>
  <section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Where the build is at / October 3, 2026</p><h2>A working desktop campaign; more to come</h2><div class="grid"><div><h3>Five chapters</h3><p>Play through the hospital, roadside evacuation, museum, service tunnels, and final mission. The campaign has combat, environmental hazards, clues, checkpoints, and two endings.</p></div><div><h3>First finish, then additions</h3><p>The current goal was a dependable desktop version. More detailed gore, expanded sound, optional chapter content, and bigger crash and finale set pieces are saved for later.</p></div><div><h3>The notes</h3><p>{entries.length} notes trace the builds and decisions we can verify, from the first surviving room on September 29 through this campaign build.</p></div></div></section>
</Base>
